Article 985 of the Civil Code: Where a beneficiary gains an improper benefit without legal basis, the person who suffers loss may request the beneficiary to return the gained benefit, except where any of the following circumstances exist:  
(1) Payments made to fulfill moral obligations;  
(2) Payments made before the due date of a debt;  
(3) Payments made in good faith to settle a debt when no obligation to pay exists.

